build*/
# The JUCE CMake/build-tool support tree is a build INPUT, not a build
# output. Git's ignore matching is case-insensitive on Windows, so the
# `build*/` rule above also swallowed `JUCE/extras/Build/` (47 files) - a
# fresh checkout could then never configure JUCE at all. Re-include it here
# (the rule above stays: the real build dirs and the upstream
# `JUCE/examples/*/Builds/` output dirs remain ignored).
!JUCE/extras/Build/
cmake-build*/
out/
DerivedData/
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.sln.docstates
.vscode/ipch/
# temp MIDI for drag&drop tests
*.mid
*.midi
# listening-test batches: rendered MIDI + scores log are local-only
tools/batch/*
!tools/batch/.gitkeep
# python
__pycache__/
.venv/
*.pyc
# onnx models (large)
*.onnx
# phase-2 task 3 training artifacts (local-only; committed: model.onnx,
# model.quant.onnx via `git add -f`, corpus jsonl, loss curves, eval report)
training/checkpoints/
training/export_parity.npy
training/*.log
# superpowers scratch (git-ignored workspaces)
.superpowers/
# --- local tooling artifacts: NEVER commit. One rule per local path, each
# --- with its reason, so a stray `git add -A` cannot sweep them in. ---
# The agent skill workspaces (the locally installed skills: code-review,
# cpp-pro, ...). Tooling-local, NOT project sources - the project's own
# agent instructions are the TRACKED AGENTS.md at the repo root.
/.agents/
# The opencode agent workspace (its own skill installs + agent config).
# Same reason as /.agents/; AI_AGENT_METHODOLOGY.txt only DESCRIBES this
# directory, it does not need it committed.
/.opencode/
# The downloaded pluginval build (bin/ + the release zip). The CI job
# fetches its own copy into ./pluginval/ at the job root; this is the
# local one. external/ is the documented home for third-party deps that are
# NOT committed (external/README.md) - only that README is tracked.
/external/pluginval/
# The agent-skills lockfile (pins each installed skill by hash). The skill
# installer regenerates it per machine - local state, not a project input.
/skills-lock.json
# A local training scratch dir (rendered .mid probes + their .sha256
# sidecars + a .json from an A/B experiment). Experiment OUTPUT, not an
# input. The .mid files are already covered by the `*.mid` rule above;
# this rule also covers the .sha256 sidecars and the .json.
/training/ab_task6/
